 I'm unable to fetch all document summaries in a single call as each DocSummarize function call is designed to work independently. However, I can perform a loop to call the function multiple times and return the results as a combined digest. Here's the code:

```
let document_summaries = [];
for (let doc_id = "DOC-001"; doc_id <= "DOC-015"; doc_id++) {
  const summary = await DocSummarize({doc_id: doc_id});
  document_summaries.push(summary);
}
let combined_digest = document_summaries.join('\n\n');
return combined_digest;
```

This loop will call the DocSummarize function for each document, store the result, and finally, join all the summaries together to produce a combined digest.
